{
 "about": "Where to read each business term (BT) of EN 16931 in a CII or UBL invoice, and the computations of the totals and VAT rules. A path is a list of element local names from the root (from the group's element for a group's terms), '|' for alternatives, '[@attr=value]' to filter on an attribute; the first match counts. A computation adds or subtracts its parts in order, and '×' multiplies by a rate in percent; with 'each', it runs once per group item (a VAT breakdown) kept by 'where', reads its unscoped parts and its result from that item, and keeps only the items of a scoped part whose terms match the item's ('match'); 'round' gives the decimals of the expected amount, rounded half away from zero. Read by lintvoice and by the lintvoice.com check page, so both show the same values.",
